#doc (Manual) "Preliminaries" =>

This section fixes the logic, its models and its algebra $`F_0`, and the two
families of variable-free formulas the later sections are about: the
Rieger–Nishimura rungs $`t_n` and the gaps $`g_k`.  It ends with the dichotomy
that splits $`F_0` at $`\bigcirc\bot`.  Everything here was in the repository
before the work this document reports; it is restated so that the later
sections can be read on their own.

# Propositional lax logic

Formulas are built from propositional variables and $`\bot` by $`\land`,
$`\lor`, $`\twoheadrightarrow` and $`\bigcirc`.  Write $`\lnot A` for
$`A \twoheadrightarrow \bot` and $`\top` for $`\bot \twoheadrightarrow \bot`.
Provability $`\Gamma \vdash A`, for a list $`\Gamma` of formulas, is natural
deduction: the intuitionistic rules with $`\bot`-elimination, and for the
modality

$$`\dfrac{\Gamma \vdash A}{\Gamma \vdash \bigcirc A}\;(\bigcirc I) \qquad\qquad \dfrac{\Gamma \vdash \bigcirc A \qquad A, \Gamma \vdash \bigcirc B}{\Gamma \vdash \bigcirc B}\;(\bigcirc E)`

following {cite}`FairtloughMendler1997`.  In Lean the derivations form a type
family, with one constructor per rule.

