# The modality is a nucleus

A _nucleus_ on a Heyting algebra $`H` is a map $`j : H \to H` with
$`a \le j a`, $`j j a \le j a` and $`j(a \land b) = j a \land j b`; nuclei are
the modal operators of {cite}`Macnab1981` and, on the algebra of truth values
of a topos, the Lawvere–Tierney topologies that {cite}`Goldblatt1981` reads as
a modality.  The rules of $`\bigcirc` give these laws on the Lindenbaum
algebra: unit, multiplication and the meet law are derivable
outright, and $`\bigcirc` is monotone (the converse of the meet law follows
from monotonicity).  PROVED.

