# Constraint models

A constraint model {pcite}`FairtloughMendler1997` has two preorders on its
worlds, an intuitionistic $`R_i` and a modal $`R_m \subseteq R_i`; a set of
_fallible_ worlds, closed upwards along $`R_i`, at which $`\bot` and therefore
every formula holds; and a valuation that is hereditary along $`R_i` and full
on the fallible worlds.  Implication is read along $`R_i` as usual, and the
modality by the clause

$$`w \Vdash \bigcirc A \iff \text{for every } v \text{ with } w \mathrel{R_i} v \text{ there is } u \text{ with } v \mathrel{R_m} u \text{ and } u \Vdash A.`

