# The Rieger–Nishimura rungs

The free Heyting algebra on one generator $`p` was described by
{cite}`Rieger1949` and {cite}`Nishimura1960`: its elements are $`\top` and the
_rungs_

$$`r_0 = \bot,\quad r_1 = p,\quad r_2 = \lnot p,\quad r_{2k+3} = r_{2k+1} \lor r_{2k+2},\quad r_{2k+4} = r_{2k+3} \twoheadrightarrow r_{2k+1},`

which are pairwise not interderivable.  The library's presentation of the
rungs is the recursion just displayed.

