{docstring sat_rn_odd +allowMissing}

{srcLink}`sat_rn_odd`

{stmt}`sat_rn_even`

{docstring sat_rn_even +allowMissing}

{srcLink}`sat_rn_even`

The ladder is lifted to a constraint model by adding one fallible world above
every world and one modal step from $`0` to it, so that $`\bigcirc\bot` holds
exactly where $`p` did; on the lift each $`t_n` has the truth set of $`r_n`.
So derivability between the $`t_n` is inclusion of truth sets on the ladder,
and distinct rungs give distinct elements of $`F_0`.  Both PROVED: the map
$`n \mapsto t_n` is an order embedding of the Rieger–Nishimura ladder into
$`F_0`.

