# The gaps

The odd rungs form a chain $`t_1 < t_3 < t_5 < \cdots`, and so do their
images $`\bigcirc t_1 \le \bigcirc t_3 \le \cdots` under the nucleus.  The
_gap_ at level $`k` says that $`\bigcirc` adds nothing at that level:

{stmt}`gap`

{docstring gap +allowMissing}

{srcLink}`gap`

The gaps from $`g_2` on are pairwise incomparable, so $`F_0` has an infinite
antichain and infinite width.  PROVED.  The countermodels are the
_edged lifts_ $`\mathcal{E}_m`: the lifted ladder with one more modal step,
from world $`m + 3` to world $`0`.  On $`\mathcal{E}_m` the gap $`g_k` fails at
world $`m + 3` when $`k \in \{m+1, m+2\}` and holds at every world otherwise;
for $`j \ne k` an edge level can be chosen with $`k` in its window and $`j`
outside it.

