# The dichotomy

Every variable-free formula lies above $`\bigcirc\bot` or below
$`\lnot\bigcirc\bot`, and never both.  PROVED.  The proof is a structural
induction; the only modal ingredient is $`\bigcirc\bot \vdash \bigcirc X`,
and the case with content is implication: if $`X` is above $`\bigcirc\bot` and
$`Y` below $`\lnot\bigcirc\bot`, then $`X \twoheadrightarrow Y` is below
$`\lnot\bigcirc\bot`.

